# =====================================================================
# Claude Code
# =====================================================================
# The .claude/ development kit IS shipped — it is how every clone of this
# repo, and every session in it, inherits the 2plot network's behavioral
# contract, skills and sandbox settings (the F1 fabric build, 2026-08-24).
# The blanket `.claude/` ignore that stood here kept all of it local-only,
# so the contract reached nobody. Allow-list, not blanket ignore: a
# directory-level ignore cannot be re-included beneath it, hence the /*
# form. Everything NOT listed stays local — this repo's `migration/` split
# packet, the `.pypirc` upload credential, session scratch, screenshots and
# settings.local.json (per-seat model overrides).
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/

# Handoff notes for work that belongs in ANOTHER repo — the kickoff docs
# that start a session elsewhere. Local scratch by design: a task list for
# 2plot.dev or the hub has no business in this checkout.
kickoff/

# Session working documents are LOCAL BY CONVENTION, network-wide: sync
# reports, handoffs and kickoff briefs name hosts, topology and process. Two
# public fleet repos were caught tracking theirs (2026-08-24). This repo's
# X402-SYNC-REPORT.md was held back by .git/info/exclude — a per-clone rule
# that protects one checkout and no fork, which is why the rule belongs
# here instead.
X402-SYNC-REPORT.md
HANDOFF-*.md
KICKOFF-*.md

# Env
.env

# Credentials — never commit PyPI upload tokens
.pypirc

# Analytics
visitor_analytics.json
visitor_analytics.json.lock
visitor_analytics.json.tmp
flask_session/
clerk_events.jsonl
security_blocklist.json
